From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0410-net-01-tensor-background.patch

Source: 0410-net-01-tensor-background.patch
matrix program until it is built

T26 can already run Ocarina of Time's Max Resolution network with two env lines, no patch. Checked
off the console on the real program, from the game's own agl_ndsr_vr_light.pck at 0x1be00: 1456
instructions, 192 HMMA, the first at 0xc00. Lichii's lowering of those bytes hashes to
6bd913e1f34e83eb, the program in the PS5 Linux log, and with 0x1b00 shared and 128x1x1 threads to
that log's pipeline 77aceefc7a77c554. This tree with EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=compact and
EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_ONLY=c00 lowers it to 3131 instructions. Against Lichii's 3071 only the 15 gathers
differ, by reading R2 and R3 where Lichii loads the same two constants, and one branch offset. The
real translator and SPIR-V backend then give 192 TensorMulAdd, 15 gathers with constant offsets and
SPIR-V that spirv-val accepts. Pointer tables on or off give the same module.

What is left is what a first run costs. Runtime compute pipelines build on a worker, but
ComputePipeline::Configure records a wait for it, so the scheduler stops with every frame behind
it: 12 s in the PS5 Linux log, 15.7 s in run60. If the driver refuses the pipeline the dispatch is
skipped with no stand-in, and the output image keeps what it held.

EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_BACKGROUND=1: while a software matrix program's pipeline is not built, and for good
if the driver refused it, RasterizerVulkan::DispatchCompute throws a text with "matrix multiply" in
it. KeplerCompute::DispatchNativeCompute then runs the stand-in, as for a rejected program. No
freeze, the stand-in's picture meanwhile, and one line when the program takes over: "Software
matrix pipeline ready: the program itself runs now". A new Shader::Info flag, uses_software_matrix,
set with TensorMulAdd, names these programs. The SPIR-V of the network is byte for byte the same.

Risk that stays: one graphics queue, no preemption. A dispatch that never ends blocks everything
until RADV calls the device lost after 10 s without progress (RADV_PS5_STALL_NS). This program has
no backward branch, its helper loop runs 8 times, and all six barriers lie outside its one branch
region, with its only early EXIT after them. That is read from the code, not run.

Off: one static bool test per compute dispatch, nothing else. Clang syntax check on the PS5 target,
exit 0, no warning in the changed lines. Not built, not run.

